# Line-ending law: the Tier-A eval artifacts are BYTE-COMPARED by the committed-artifacts
# drift detector (`ReplayDeterminismTest`). On a checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` the
# default CRLF smudge made the working file differ from the LF the harness writes, so
# `./gradlew test` failed on line endings alone (the verifier's Stage-3 finding). Force LF
# for these artifacts so the detector compares content, not the platform's checkout style.
.state/eval/*.json text eol=lf
.state/eval/*.md text eol=lf
